From: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] laguna: emit the attention gate adjacent to Q/K/V so it joins the grouped matvec

Port of the R9700 laguna-xs series' 0020 to the GB10 CUDA track. This
track's README already diagnosed the blocker and stopped one step short of
fixing it: attn_gate is the least efficient launch in the whole decode
(72 rows, 0.235 MB, 6.3 us, 37 GB/s) and it is "rejected by the
hoist-legality range check, not by type or shape".

The refusal is the ALLOCATOR's doing, not the detector's. All four attention
projections read the same post-attn_norm activation, but the DFS reaches the
gate only through the post-attention multiply, so stock emits attn_gate_proj
well after Qcur - and by then ggml-alloc has handed it a block that one of
the grouped destinations writes. 0001's hoist check sees the overlap and
correctly refuses. No backend change can fix that; the node has to be
emitted while nothing else in the group is live.

One ggml_build_forward_expand does it, gated on the decode shape
(attn_inp->ne[1] == 1; at prefill the projections are GEMMs and the grouped
matvec never applies). Pure reordering of independent work: ops, operands
and shapes are untouched, and the grouped kernel gives every row exactly the
thread geometry, k-loop and reduction sequence of its individual launch.
Bit-identical by construction - which, after this track's round 1, is the
property that matters most (see the README).

GGML_LAGUNA_QKV_GATE_PIN=0 restores stock order (same-binary control);
=2 selects the reorder-Q/K/V-too variant that the R9700 twin measured as a
trap (it costs the grouped rope and set_rows launches and moves decode-path
perplexity 0.5%), kept selectable so the rejection stays reproducible.
diff --git a/src/models/laguna.cpp b/src/models/laguna.cpp
index 82c9a95..37e6be3 100644
--- a/src/models/laguna.cpp
+++ b/src/models/laguna.cpp
@@ -208,7 +208,48 @@ llama_model_laguna::graph::graph(const llama_model & model, const llm_graph_para
             // g_proj on the *pre-attention* hidden state (matches HF
             // reference: gate is computed from the same `hidden_states`
             // input as q/k/v, not from the attn output).
+            //
+            // GRAPH ORDER, not arithmetic. All four projections read the same
+            // post-attn_norm activation, but the DFS reaches the gate only
+            // through the post-attention multiply, so stock emits
+            // attn_gate_proj well after Qcur - and by then ggml-alloc has
+            // handed it a block one of the grouped destinations writes. 0001's
+            // hoist-legality range check sees the overlap and correctly refuses
+            // to group it. The refusal is the ALLOCATOR's doing, not the
+            // detector's, so no backend change can fix it; the node has to be
+            // emitted while nothing else in the group is live.
+            //
+            // One ggml_build_forward_expand does that. Pure reordering of
+            // independent work: ops, operands and shapes are untouched, and the
+            // grouped kernel gives every row exactly the thread geometry,
+            // k-loop and reduction sequence of its individual launch, so the
+            // result is bit-identical by construction.
+            //
+            // Mode 2 additionally pins Q/K/V. On the R9700 twin that variant
+            // let more projections join but cost the grouped rope and grouped
+            // set_rows launches and moved decode-path perplexity by 0.5%; it is
+            // kept selectable so the rejection stays reproducible rather than
+            // being rediscovered.
+            static const int qkv_gate_pin = [] {
+                const char * e = getenv("GGML_LAGUNA_QKV_GATE_PIN");
+                return e == nullptr ? 1 : atoi(e);
+            }();
+
+            // decode shape only: at prefill the projections are GEMMs, the
+            // grouped matvec never applies, and the reorder would only perturb
+            // the allocator for no gain. attn_inp->ne[1] is n_tokens.
+            const bool pin_decode_shape = attn_inp->ne[1] == 1;
+
+            if (qkv_gate_pin >= 2 && pin_decode_shape) {
+                ggml_build_forward_expand(gf, Qcur);
+                ggml_build_forward_expand(gf, Kcur);
+                ggml_build_forward_expand(gf, Vcur);
+            }
+
             ggml_tensor * gate = build_lora_mm(model.layers[il].wqkv_gate, attn_inp);
+            if (qkv_gate_pin >= 1 && pin_decode_shape) {
+                ggml_build_forward_expand(gf, gate);
+            }
             cb(gate, "attn_gate_proj", il);
 
             // QK RMSNorm at head_dim level (Qwen3 style)
